# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#169-e), L §4.4: a sum's term that a window leaves open (days_between to dk[a], a window) makes the
# sum the window's hole, named by the day it comes from. 2.1.7's refcore refused the addition (RUN-DOMAIN 0 +
# window(59, 68)). T's fixes/p60/sum_days_win.
=== m.tally
model pw
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
kind mixed: place any signed
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place wallet: mixed lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input dk[k in ks]: date
input d0: date
input dd: int

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dd)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  d0 = 2026-01-01 "s"
  dd = 10 "s"
  dk[a] = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10) "s"
  dk[b] = 2026-03-05 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask q: sum(days_between(d0, dk[k]) for k in ks)
=== expect
q: ?"date within window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a term of sum" (dk[a])
  cut 2026-04-25
warning: WARN-UNREAD place wallet is read by nothing
